{"abstract":"Given a set of n points in the Euclidean plane, the k-MinSumRadius problem asks to cover this point set using k disks with the objective of minimizing the sum of the radii of the disks. After a long line of research on related problems, it was finally discovered that this problem admits a polynomial time algorithm [GKKPV’12]; however, the running time of this algorithm is O(n881), and its relevance is thereby mostly of theoretical nature. A practically and structurally interesting special case of the k-MinSumRadius problem is that of small k. For the 2-MinSumRadius problem, a near-quadratic time algorithm with expected running time O(n2 log2 n log2 log n) was given over 30 years ago [Eppstein’92]. We present the first improvement of this result, namely, a near-linear time algorithm to compute the 2-MinSumRadius that runs in expected O(n log2 n log2 log n) time. We generalize this result to any constant dimension d, for which we give an O(n2−1/(⌈d/2⌉+1)+ε) time algorithm. Additionally, we give a near-quadratic time algorithm for 3-MinSumRadius in the plane that runs in expected O(n2 log2 n log2 log n) time. All of these algorithms rely on insights that uncover a surprisingly simple structure of optimal solutions: we can specify a linear number of lines out of which one separates one of the clusters from the remaining clusters in an optimal solution.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Abrahamsen, Mikkel","de Berg, Sarita","Meijer, Lucas","Nusser, André","Theocharous, Leonidas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777792"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-14","place":"Athens, gr","start":"2024-06-11","title":"40th International Symposium on Computational Geometry, SoCG 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["Geometric clustering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clustering with few disks to minimize the sum of radii","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2024.2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-777792","identifier":[{"id":"85195503476","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5a347906-4730-4ef2-921b-a403fcc62a8f"],"keyword":["covering points with disks","geometric clustering","minimize sum of radii"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-6727AC073682D63078357F0560A1E9D4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2024.2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/413646433/LIPIcs.SoCG.2024.2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"abrahamsenpau","last":"Abrahamsen","locid":"63596832-461f-409a-a2cc-81023b9b8e46","name":"Abrahamsen, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0003-2734-4690","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sarita","key":"debergpau","last":"de Berg","name":"de Berg, Sarita","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lucas","key":"meijerpau","last":"Meijer","name":"Meijer, Lucas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"André","key":"nusserpau","last":"Nusser","locid":"03d129b6-407b-438d-a727-efd67507d253","name":"Nusser, André","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Leonidas","key":"theocharouspau","last":"Theocharous","name":"Theocharous, Leonidas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.socg.2024.2","issn":["18688969"],"journal":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","paperid":"2","status":"p","title":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","title_org":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","volume":"293"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85195503476"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5a347906-4730-4ef2-921b-a403fcc62a8f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Clustering with Few Disks to Minimize the Sum of Radii","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-777792","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
